    <item>
      <title>A Political Breakdown That Dare Not Speak Its Name</title>
      <link>https://www.bloomberg.com/opinion/articles/2026-10-27/a-political-breakdown-that-dare-not-speak-its-name</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">872f4d3cfb4a97ce2abb4f9a</guid>
      <pubDate>Tue, 27 Oct 2026 09:30:19 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>The most pressing policy question facing the US — how to restore fiscal control — has been conspicuously absent in campaigning for the midterm elections. Neither party is willing to frame a plausible way to solve the problem, so they’ve seemingly agreed not to discuss it. Their silence is an abject failure of governance. One wonders how much longer Washington will be able to get away with it.</description>
      <dc:creator>Clive Crook</dc:creator>
