      <title>India’s eMudhra Exposes a Weak Link in Internet Security</title>
      <link>https://www.bloomberg.com/opinion/articles/2026-10-26/india-s-emudhra-exposes-a-weak-link-in-internet-security</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">e3c805b5851185b0697c1554</guid>
      <pubDate>Mon, 26 Oct 2026 20:01:06 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>Trust on the internet is supposed to be one of the marvels of modern cryptography. A malicious website may try to impersonate your bank or email provider, but web browsers are designed to block the fake. The encryption behind the padlock in the address bar is so strong that even supercomputers running for millennia wouldn’t be able to break it.</description>
